   "content": "**South Korea ranks second in research spending and first in researchers.**\n\n- **Research spending:** 4.94% of GDP (2023), behind only Israel (6.35%).\n- **Researchers:** 9,472 per million people (2023), the most of 101 countries.\n\nThe dashboard shows both top-10 rankings with South Korea highlighted; a world map beside it shows researchers per million people everywhere. Each country's latest figure from 2020–2024; territories under 100,000 people left out. Source: UIS, February 2026 release; indicators EXPGDP.TOT, RESDEN.INHAB.TFTE.",
